From f5a0cbb14a1c5250771999809af8254eb491ed36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 09:23:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AGS] Add a RIFF WAV + Creative VOC loader for DOS (Sound
 milestone S1)

SDL2_sound is gated out on DOS (patch 0006) -- AGS's real clip formats
that stay in scope for native DOS playback are WAV/VOC only (OGG/MP3 are
host-pre-converted per PLAN.md's Sound milestone decision 2, tracker
formats are S6's own question). Rather than port SDL2_sound, this adds
a small standalone loader: sniffs the actual file header (RIFF/WAVE or
"Creative Voice File") regardless of the clip's own extension or
fileType hint -- PLAN.md's own requirement, since v361_objnames games
can carry an unreliable fileName/fileType pairing -- and decodes
whatever PCM it contains.

Supported sub-formats: WAV PCM (format tag 1) 8/16-bit; VOC codec 0
(unsigned 8-bit, old format) and type-9 new-format signed 16-bit, plus
type 2 (continuation), 3 (silence), 8 (extended/stereo) blocks. Loop
markers (type 6/7) are read past but not honored -- AGS's own clip-level
`repeat` flag already covers whole-clip looping, and a mid-file VOC loop
is a rare authoring feature not needed for this milestone. Anything else
(ADPCM, mu-law, a genuinely corrupt file, or a WAV/VOC sub-format this
loader doesn't recognize) fails cleanly, matching how a missing decoder
already fails today ("AudioClip.Play: unable to load sound file").

Every clip is resampled/downmixed ONCE, at decode time, to the mixer's
fixed device format (dos_audio_mixer.h, previous patch) via linear
interpolation -- adequate for the short SFX/chime-class content this
decoder handles; real music is MIDI/tracker, later Sound-milestone
slices. This is dossage's own 0039 lesson applied up front: converting
per-chunk cost 43% of every frame there until it moved to load time.

Nothing calls this yet -- wired into sdldecoder.cpp in the next patch.
Standalone and independently buildable, same as the mixer patch.
